## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to diagnose cross-region performance issues with multiple plausible culprits and limited signal.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region latency, QUIC, ECMP, in-cache hot keys, path validation.
- Observability: RTT, path changes, queueing, cache stats.
- Mitigation: pacing, caching strategy, hashing stability.

## Code Example
```javascript
function preventStampede(key) {
  // simple mutex-like guard
  if (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);
  acquireLock(key);
  try { /* refresh */ return value; } finally { releaseLock(key); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate cache-stampede vs QUIC path changes with data you collect?
- What changes would you prioritize first in a live system?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to diagnose production latency where security tooling (TLS inspection) interacts with edge caches and rate limits.

## Key Concepts

- TLS inspection overhead and queueing
- Firewall connection limits and burst behavior
- Edge CDN caching and TTLs
- Observability: edge logs, pcap, and curl timing data

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple latency probe using fetch
async function probe(url){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  await fetch(url);
  const t1 = performance.now();
  console.log('latency', t1 - t0);
}
probe('https://edge.example/login');
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify bypass granularity while maintaining security?
- What metrics would you monitor during a peak event to alert on this issue?
